{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015GSDf72znFEbDjPBEYVdN5","type":"tool_result","content":"# AAAI 2025 Statistics Summary\n\nBased on the webpage content:\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- **Total Submissions:** 12,957\n- **Accepted Papers:** 3,032 (23.40% acceptance rate)\n- **Rejected Papers:** 3,182 (24.56%)\n\n**Scoring Information:**\nThe page indicates a scoring scale ranging from 1.00 to 8.00. According to the data presented, \"min:4.50max:8.00 avg:6.21std:0.96\" represents overall submission scores.\n\n**Score Comparison:**\nThe accepted papers show a mean rating of 5.72, while the overall average across all submissions is 6.21. This suggests accepted papers actually scored below the conference average, though the page notes that \"official and community scores are both available\" and doesn't explicitly separate accepted versus rejected paper averages.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nThe webpage emphasizes that \"reject\" counts reflect \"only submissions that opted in for public release,\" meaning the visible rejection statistics may underrepresent actual rejections. The data also includes community form responses (480 responses, 447 valid) alongside official OpenReview metrics."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"176da81f-308c-4dd6-ae97-a751123aff6c","uuid":"95a421a9-38bb-4f0e-9d77-e6681dde0422","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:42:35.985Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":213994,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# AAAI 2025 Statistics Summary\n\nBased on the webpage content:\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n- **Total Submissions:** 12,957\n- **Accepted Papers:** 3,032 (23.40% acceptance rate)\n- **Rejected Papers:** 3,182 (24.56%)\n\n**Scoring Information:**\nThe page indicates a scoring scale ranging from 1.00 to 8.00. According to the data presented, \"min:4.50max:8.00 avg:6.21std:0.96\" represents overall submission scores.\n\n**Score Comparison:**\nThe accepted papers show a mean rating of 5.72, while the overall average across all submissions is 6.21. This suggests accepted papers actually scored below the conference average, though the page notes that \"official and community scores are both available\" and doesn't explicitly separate accepted versus rejected paper averages.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nThe webpage emphasizes that \"reject\" counts reflect \"only submissions that opted in for public release,\" meaning the visible rejection statistics may underrepresent actual rejections. The data also includes community form responses (480 responses, 447 valid) alongside official OpenReview metrics.","durationMs":4969,"url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/aaai-statistics/aaai-2025-statistics/"}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YSkPq6sGBAhfS1J5ttXWtN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough to proceed. Based on my search:\n\n- AAAI uses a 1-10 scale for overall assessment\n- AAAI 2025 had ~23.4% acceptance rate, 12,957 submissions\n- AAAI 2026 had ~23,000 submissions\n- The review dimensions include: soundness, novelty, significance, clarity, relevance\n- Average scores for accepted papers tend to be around 5.7-6.2\n\nThe standard AAAI review form (based on OpenReview) uses:\n- Overall Assessment: 1-10 scale\n\n\n- Confidence: 1-5\n- Soundness, Significance, Novelty, Clarity as dimensions\n\nThe scale maps to: 1 for trivial/wrong, 2-4 for various reject levels, 5 for borderline reject, 6 for weak accept, 7 for accept, 8 for clear accept, 9 for strong accept, and 10 for top-tier seminal work. Now I'm ready to dispatch the two reviewers in parallel—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work.\n\nI'm setting up a four-stage review process: independent evaluations first, then cross-sharing of perspectives, convergence toward consensus, and finally a consolidated report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":71127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"176da81f-308c-4dd6-ae97-a751123aff6c","uuid":"132cb6fa-da95-40d6-af54-6890259b254b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YSkPq6sGBAhfS1J5ttXWtN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the AAAI scoring context. Now dispatching two parallel reviewers: R1 (Methods + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":71127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"176da81f-308c-4dd6-ae97-a751123aff6c","uuid":"af737f99-96d5-4b6a-8393-7bfdf47c425f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YSkPq6sGBAhfS1J5ttXWtN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sj5AAPc2wMD3j1ppyboeDc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a blind peer review of an academic paper submitted to AAAI 2027. Your focus areas are **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## AAAI Review Criteria\nAAAI uses a 1-10 overall assessment scale. Acceptance rate ~23%. Dimensions: soundness, significance, novelty, clarity, relevance. The review form asks for a paper summary, strengths, weaknesses, questions for authors, and an overall score.\n\nScale:\n- 10: Top 5%, seminal\n- 9: Strong accept\n- 8: Clear accept\n- 7: Accept, good paper with minor weaknesses\n- 6: Weak accept / borderline\n- 5: Borderline / weak reject\n- 4: Reject, below threshold\n- 3: Clear reject\n- 2: Strong reject\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"Distributional Fingerprints of Generation Depth: Detecting Recursive LLM Contamination Beyond Binary Classification\"\n\nThe paper introduces \"distributional fingerprinting\" for estimating the generation depth of text (gen-0/gen-1/gen-2+) by measuring distributional divergence from human text under a small reference LM. It tests two hypotheses about non-paraphrastic generation chains: convergence (H1) vs monotonic divergence (H2), confirming H2. A 7-feature classifier (5 reference-model entropy features + 2 surface features) with XGBoost achieves macro-F1=0.87 (3-class) and generalizes across 5 generators (leave-one-out F1=0.78). Depth-aware data filtering retains 42% data at near-human perplexity, outperforming binary baselines by 5.2%.\n\n## Key Results (from paper)\n- Table 1: Feature ablation — ref-only F1=0.79, surface-only F1=0.63, full F1=0.87, delta=+0.16\n- Table 2: Permutation importance — entropy_mean=0.28 (top), hapax_ratio drops from 0.30 XGB gain to 0.14 permutation\n- Table 3: Leave-one-generator-out — mean F1=0.78±0.03 across 5 generators\n- Table 4: Per-generator in-distribution — pooled F1=0.86\n- Table 5: Cross-reference models — Pythia-410M F1=0.86, OLMo-2-1B F1=0.76, Qwen3.5-0.8B F1=0.74, ensemble F1=0.88\n- Table 6: Paraphrastic vs continuation — continuation F1=0.85, paraphrastic F1=0.58, KS D=0.41 p<1e-4\n- Table 7-8: Downstream utility — depth-filtered PPL=29.0, binary baselines PPL=31.8-32.1, human PPL=28.3\n- Table 9: Prompt types — continuation F1=0.85, elaboration F1=0.80, inspired_rewriting F1=0.72, drift rate correlation ρ=0.91\n- Table 10: Cross-model chains — F1=0.75, 10-point drop from single-model\n- Table 11: Multi-domain — Wikipedia F1=0.86, News F1=0.83, Scientific F1=0.81, Creative F1=0.78, leave-one-out F1=0.77\n- Table 12: 5-class ordinal — macro-F1=0.62, Spearman ρ=0.83, MAE=0.58\n- Table 13: Robustness — 5% edit F1=0.83, 10% F1=0.78, 20% F1=0.67\n- Table 14: LD-Score integration — marginal +0.01\n- Table 15: Neural baseline — XGBoost F1=0.86/0.78 (in/cross), QLoRA F1=0.83/0.71, XGBoost 3min vs 12 GPU·h\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (what was planned)\nThe full experiment plan includes 12 experiments:\n1. feature_ablation (plan_001) — covered in paper\n2. cross_generator_evaluation (plan_002) — covered\n3. cross_family_reference_model (plan_003) — covered\n4. downstream_utility (plan_004) — covered\n5. prompt_type_comparison (plan_005) — covered\n6. paraphrastic_comparison (plan_006) — covered\n7. cross_model_chains (plan_007) — covered\n8. multi_domain_seeds (plan_008) — covered\n9. finer_grained_ordinal (plan_009) — covered\n10. human_edit_robustness (plan_010) — covered\n11. ld_score_feature (plan_011) — covered\n12. end_to_end_classifier (plan_012) — covered\n\nAll 12 planned experiments appear in the paper.\n\n## Your Task (R1: Methods + Experiments)\n\nProvide a detailed review focusing on:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness**: Are the methods technically correct? Are the experimental designs valid? Are there confounds or methodological issues?\n2. **Experimental Rigor**: Are the experiments comprehensive? Are baselines appropriate? Are statistical tests used correctly? Is there proper cross-validation?\n3. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to reproduce the results?\n4. **Specific Technical Concerns**: Any issues with feature design, classifier choice, evaluation metrics, etc.\n5. **Missing Experiments or Baselines**: What's not covered that should be?\n\nFormat your review as:\n\n### Paper Summary (2-3 sentences)\n### Strengths (bulleted)\n### Weaknesses (bulleted)\n### Questions for Authors (bulleted)\n### Missing Experiments/Concerns\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/10\n- Experimental Rigor: X/10\n- Reproducibility: X/10\n- Overall (Methods+Experiments focus): X/10\n- Confidence: X/5\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":71127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"176da81f-308c-4dd6-ae97-a751123aff6c","uuid":"590a631a-01a3-4cc5-acab-d3c073a735c3"}
